// Title: HackTool - GodPotato Execution
// Sigma ID: 2a5a2f2c-9936-41e7-948c-13f96936c7a2
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Ashish Pulivarthy (ashish-cybersec)
// Date: 2026-11-11 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: privilege-escalation, stealth, T1134.001
// Description: Detects the execution of GodPotato, a privilege escalation tool that abuses a flaw in how the
//   RPCSS service handles OXID resolution over DCOM. It escalates from an account that holds the
//   SeImpersonatePrivilege token privilege, such as a web or database service account, to SYSTEM. It
//   affects Windows 8 through Windows 11 and Windows Server 2012 through Windows Server 2022.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate files with these rare hacktool names
// References:
//   - https://github.com/BeichenDream/GodPotato
//   - https://www.ic3.gov/CSA/2025/250219.pdf
//   - https://unit42.paloaltonetworks.com/manic-menagerie-targets-web-hosting-and-it/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/4994679357c5771693dd94dc81c29058b71ac7d6/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_hktl_godpotato.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ((FolderPath contains "\\GodPotato-" and FolderPath contains ".exe") or FolderPath endswith "\\GodPotato.exe") or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "GodPotato.exe"
